1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:03,880
Yeya, growing between the lines.

2
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:07,680
Yeya is a reader for books you import yourself.

3
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:09,330
Adjust the page to suit you,

4
00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:12,672
make notes, or carry on listening.

5
00:00:13,072 --> 00:00:15,909
Import EPUB, PDF, text,

6
00:00:15,909 --> 00:00:19,097
Markdown, or supported Kindle files.

7
00:00:19,097 --> 00:00:21,572
Use Files, send books over Wi-Fi,

8
00:00:21,572 --> 00:00:25,172
or connect a cloud drive or WebDAV.

9
00:00:25,572 --> 00:00:27,997
Choose the font, size, spacing,

10
00:00:27,997 --> 00:00:30,172
and background you prefer.

11
00:00:30,172 --> 00:00:32,072
You can turn pages or scroll,

12
00:00:32,072 --> 00:00:35,130
depending on how you like to read.

13
00:00:35,530 --> 00:00:37,280
Mark a sentence with a highlight,

14
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:40,630
underline, or circle, and add a note.

15
00:00:40,630 --> 00:00:44,547
Open that record later to return to the passage.

16
00:00:44,947 --> 00:00:46,684
When you want a break from the screen,

17
00:00:46,684 --> 00:00:49,972
open the player and listen from your current place.

18
00:00:49,972 --> 00:00:53,297
It carries on into the next chapter.

19
00:00:53,697 --> 00:00:55,359
Choose a voice from your device,

20
00:00:55,359 --> 00:00:57,159
install an offline voice pack,

21
00:00:57,159 --> 00:01:00,588
or connect an online speech service.

22
00:01:00,988 --> 00:01:05,601
Kokoro and VITS are among the adapted offline voice packs.

23
00:01:05,601 --> 00:01:07,988
Download from ModelScope or Hugging Face,

24
00:01:07,988 --> 00:01:10,963
then listen without a connection.

25
00:01:11,363 --> 00:01:13,126
Online options include Edge,

26
00:01:13,126 --> 00:01:15,363
OpenAI, MiniMax, Doubao,

27
00:01:15,363 --> 00:01:21,172
and Azure. You can also configure a compatible custom endpoint.

28
00:01:21,572 --> 00:01:23,172
Change the speed or voice,

29
00:01:23,172 --> 00:01:25,997
and set a sleep timer when you need one.

30
00:01:25,997 --> 00:01:30,588
Playback continues with the player closed or the screen locked.

31
00:01:30,988 --> 00:01:34,688
Turn on bilingual reading for a book in another language.

32
00:01:34,688 --> 00:01:37,151
The translation appears beneath the original,

33
00:01:37,151 --> 00:01:40,672
so you can compare a sentence while you read.

34
00:01:41,072 --> 00:01:43,997
Ask about a sentence you don't understand.

35
00:01:43,997 --> 00:01:45,734
Follow up on the explanation,

36
00:01:45,734 --> 00:01:47,834
request a more natural translation,

37
00:01:47,834 --> 00:01:50,838
or change how a term is worded.

38
00:01:51,238 --> 00:01:53,263
Tell the AI you want larger text,

39
00:01:53,263 --> 00:01:54,888
more space between lines,

40
00:01:54,888 --> 00:01:56,988
or a warmer background.

41
00:01:56,988 --> 00:02:01,255
It changes the reader settings and reports what changed.

42
00:02:01,655 --> 00:02:04,318
Ask the AI to underline a sentence in the book,

43
00:02:04,318 --> 00:02:06,755
like the green wavy line here.

44
00:02:06,755 --> 00:02:08,705
You can change the style or color,

45
00:02:08,705 --> 00:02:10,963
or add a note.

46
00:02:11,363 --> 00:02:15,376
For a growing library, ask the AI for a folder plan.

47
00:02:15,376 --> 00:02:17,038
Check where each book would go,

48
00:02:17,038 --> 00:02:20,838
edit the folder names, and apply the plan.

49
00:02:21,238 --> 00:02:23,226
If you only remember part of something,

50
00:02:23,226 --> 00:02:26,688
ask the AI to find it. It can look for a book,

51
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:30,672
a passage, or a saved annotation or note.

52
00:02:31,072 --> 00:02:32,859
Your records keep annotations,

53
00:02:32,859 --> 00:02:36,184
notes, and AI conversations together.

54
00:02:36,184 --> 00:02:39,259
Ask for a summary of one topic and save it as a note,

55
00:02:39,259 --> 00:02:42,130
with links to its sources.

56
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:45,068
Ask for a daily reading goal of thirty minutes,

57
00:02:45,068 --> 00:02:48,168
or tell the AI how to set your reminders.

58
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:51,330
It changes settings directly and opens fields you need to fill in

59
00:02:51,330 --> 00:02:53,380
yourself.

60
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:56,355
Each book can have a different goal.

61
00:02:56,355 --> 00:02:57,993
Read a novel for pleasure,

62
00:02:57,993 --> 00:03:00,430
study a practical book to use its ideas,

63
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:02,705
or prepare for an exam.

64
00:03:02,705 --> 00:03:05,547
Tell the AI what you want.

65
00:03:05,947 --> 00:03:09,447
The AI uses your goal and daily available time to plan reading or

66
00:03:09,447 --> 00:03:15,380
study. The Today page shows what to work on and the estimated time.

67
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:20,580
For a difficult idea, ask for another explanation or an example.

68
00:03:20,580 --> 00:03:22,718
Try explaining it in your own words,

69
00:03:22,718 --> 00:03:26,297
then use the feedback to see what you missed.

70
00:03:26,697 --> 00:03:29,872
Exercises let you check what you understood.

71
00:03:29,872 --> 00:03:31,834
Read the feedback after answering,

72
00:03:31,834 --> 00:03:34,384
and return to the supporting passage in the book when you need

73
00:03:34,384 --> 00:03:36,505
another look.

74
00:03:36,905 --> 00:03:38,343
Review what you have studied,

75
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:42,818
or take a quiz. The AI uses your saved answers and understanding

76
00:03:42,818 --> 00:03:46,380
checks to help you decide what to revisit.

77
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:51,130
Yeya, growing between the lines.
